{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod","id":784382,"title":"Homebrew idea: Batman in the WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-11T15:27:45-08:00","id":784382,"title":"Homebrew idea: Batman in the WoD","content":"It was a favorite thought experiment of my friends and I to imagine how our favorite comic book characters would fit in the World of Darkness. Back before the release of the new WoD we'd imagine Batman as a Mage who didn't realize he was awakened, which would explain how he pulled off some blatantly impossible crap in spite of being an &quot;ordinary human&quot;. Since the release of the nWoD I've re-imagined Batman as a Mortal. Perhaps even a hunter. All or most of his rogue's gallery would definitely fit in one Slasher category or another. As an amusing homebrew idea I made a character sheet for him. Then lost it. But the gist is that Batman is a peak human being, so he has 5 dots in all attributes, 5 dots in every skill, of course 10 willpower, a long list of equipment and vehicles, and a loooong list of merits that included a long ass list of contacts, a long ass list of allies, and one retainer in the form of Alfred Pennyworth (no endowments, he doesn't need them). He also has a Morality of 6 and suffers from the &quot;Suspicion&quot; derangement.<br /> <br /> Batman's villains, while not as well thought out, would fit within the following Slasher Undertakings:<br /> Joker-Maniac<br /> Harley Quinn-Psycho<br /> Two-Face-Freak<br /> Penguin-Freak<br /> Killer Croc-Mutant<br /> Mr. Freeze-Legend<br /> Riddler-Genius<br /> Poison Ivy-Avenger/Legend<br /> The Mad Hatter-Psycho<br /> <br /> If this sort of thing appeals to you, then I leave this here as an idea seed for running your own home brew Batman RPG using the Hunter: the Vigil game mechanics. You could also do something very similar with the CW version of Green Arrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","user":"Zolace","date":". 12-11-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T15:54:25-08:00","id":784393,"title":"","content":"Oh, and be honest...at one point or another we've all wanted to play a character who's character sheet was maxed out. Getting to play Batman just gives you a valid excuse to do just that. You're welcome.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T08:41:45-08:00","id":784770,"title":"","content":"Oh, I just thought of this! For extra cheezering you can give Bats my homebrew merit &quot;Success at 6&quot;, which basically states that Batman only needs to roll a 6 or higher to make a success on dice rolls instead of 8 or higher (while everyone else has to roll 8 r higher). This mechanic could be used to explain how he gets away with some seemingly impossible feats without using magic or supernatural gifts. You know, besides being a peak human. Cause let's face it, there are some feats he's been able to pull off that don't make too much sense, even for a &quot;peak human&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T10:37:25-08:00","id":784845,"title":"","content":"I've been meaning to stat up Batman and his allies as a Conspiracy. I'm pretty sure Genius is a better fit for Harley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T12:17:17-08:00","id":784895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zolace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=784770#post784770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I just thought of this! For extra cheezering you can give Bats my homebrew merit &quot;Success at 6&quot;, which basically states that Batman only needs to roll a 6 or higher to make a success on dice rolls instead of 8 or higher (while everyone else has to roll 8 r higher). This mechanic could be used to explain how he gets away with some seemingly impossible feats without using magic or supernatural gifts. You know, besides being a peak human. Cause let's face it, there are some feats he's been able to pull off that don't make too much sense, even for a &quot;peak human&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wouldn't you know it, Amechra actually suggested altering the Rote Quality into a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760194-i-don-t-really-like-rote-actions\"><b>Routine Action</b></a>, which does exactly that: Successes at 6+ on each die. I also came up with a Merit when I kept imagining ways to even the playing field between mortals and ephemeral beings:<br /> <br /> <b>Unyielding (5 Dots):</b> Your character may spend 1 willpower point to double her Resolve, Composure or Stamina when applying it as a penalty to any supernatural powers that alter thought, emotion or body. He may also spend 1 willpower point to the gain the 8 Again benefit on contested rolls against such powers. The Tolerance granted by his Conviction still applies. This Merit stacks with Indomitable. Prerequisites: No Supernatural Template, Conviction 4 (Or all Resistance Attributes at 3+ if you don't include Conviction). The rules for the Conviction Powerstat may be found on the &quot;Mirrors&quot; supplement for 1ed NWOD, pages 32 to 35.<br /> <br /> Let's say that Batman is a Hunter, thus capable of Risking Willpower. I'll give Batman a Conviction of 7 or maybe 8, which allows him to spend 3 willpower points per turn. I'll go even further and say that Batman acts almost like a Spirit: he is considered to have Professional Training 5 for all Skills that can be applied to crime-fighting somehow, but only as long as he is acting according to the Batman persona. His mindset simply won't allow for his full expertise to be used when he's being Bruce Wayne, which is practically an Unchained's Cover to him*. He can spend 1 willpower point to Risk Willpower when, say, disarming a thug. His Omni-Professional Training gives him 9 Again, which is upgraded into 8 Again by Risking Willpower. He can then spend a second willpower point to also gain Rote Quality/Routine Action, and a third to use his Conviction and gain +5 dice. All in all, he only spent 1 willpower point, without even going into the laundry list of equipment, Skill Tricks, Endowments and other Merits he's accumulated. I wouldn't go so far as to give him 5 dots in every single Attribute and Skill, though. He's not a god. However, after reading through Pendragon's Homebrew Hub, I also decided that Batman has the Prodigy Merit (which allows epic mortals to raise an Attribute or Skill to 6 dots) applied to Resolve, Stealth, Investigation and Intimidation. This would give him 1 Reversal Point for each of those stats, as defined in the &quot;Imperial Mysteries&quot; supplement for Mage 1ED, page 17.<br /> <br /> Or, you could do what Anonymous once suggested in a /tg/ thread about giving stats to Batman: he's a Game Master PC. You are not allowed to look at his sheet.<br /> <br /> I have character sheets written for him and Slasher!Joker, if anyone is interested in seeing them.<br /> <br /> *There's an idea for those who want to really emphasize the psychological rift between the Batman and Bruce Wayne. He could also be an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/660807-batman-ugallu-nemesis\"><b>Ugallu with a Hunger For Punishment</b></a>. If you use Genius: The Transgression, he could be a Klagen or Grimm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-13-2015, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T13:25:32-08:00","id":784947,"title":"","content":"Two points:<br /> 1) Having 5 dots in everything doesn't make Batman a god. Technically any ordinary human can have a maximum of 5 dots in any attribute and skill. Batman, being a peak human, would only have the maximum dots allowable for a human in any given attribute and skill, which is not *technically* super human nor god-like. IF I were going to make Batman a god I would use Scion rules and give him Epic Attributes as well as normal attributes that go well past 5, starting with giving him Intelligence 15.<br /> 2) Batman IS a god now. The god of knowledge. Have a look: <a href=\"http://io9.com/batman-learns-the-jokers-biggest-secret-in-justice-leag-1717992429\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/batman-learns-the-jok...eag-1717992429</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T18:08:53-08:00","id":785092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zolace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=784947#post784947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two points:<br /> 1) Having 5 dots in everything doesn't make Batman a god. Technically any ordinary human can have a maximum of 5 dots in any attribute and skill. Batman, being a peak human, would only have the maximum dots allowable for a human in any given attribute and skill, which is not *technically* super human nor god-like. IF I were going to make Batman a god I would use Scion rules and give him Epic Attributes as well as normal attributes that go well past 5, starting with giving him Intelligence 15.<br /> 2) Batman IS a god now. The god of knowledge. Have a look: <a href=\"http://io9.com/batman-learns-the-jokers-biggest-secret-in-justice-leag-1717992429\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/batman-learns-the-jok...eag-1717992429</a></div> </div> </div> </div> 1) OK, you got me there. I expressed myself poorly when I said that.<br /> <br /> 2) That's quite amusing, but it's more along the lines of Mage!Batman.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, if you allow Batman to have Supernatural Merits, he's a very strong candidate for Mind Of A Madman (GMC, page 173).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T18:35:58-08:00","id":785109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=784895#post784895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he is considered to have Professional Training 5 for all Skills that can be applied to crime-fighting somehow, but only as long as he is acting according to the Batman persona. His mindset simply won't allow for his full expertise to be used when he's being Bruce Wayne, which is practically an Unchained's Cover to him*.</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember an issue where Bruce used Batman's Intimidation ability during a board meeting. This was shown by Bruce casting Batman's shadow on the wall behind him, and some other Bat-family/Batman, Inc. characters have done the same. I'm tempted to stat this as an Endowment or Merit: Shadow of the Bat...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T19:01:36-08:00","id":785124,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, if you want to cut back on Batman's power level (perish the thought!), you can get a <i>pretty good</i> likeness with Cursed, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Fated Ferocity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</a>, Mind of a Madman, and <i>maybe</i> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15PLeCG-9xqTTaz66JQgLTQHE8OE6-pqsG-6NDddKzok/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Air of Menace and At Any Cost</a>.<br /> <br /> His Curse is that <i>someone</i> that he's put in prison or Arkham Asylum will escape to haunt him during the Chronicle, only to be replaced by another escapee if he manages to put them back in.<br /> <br /> That particular combination of merits gives him a +2 bonus against fear and self-doubt, makes him <i>outright immune</i> to anything that would turn him away from completing an Aspiration, makes him harder to hurt or slow down, makes him ultra-scary, and lets him read criminals like a book.<br /> <br /> Dribble on Luxury, Professional Training, and whatever merits get you neat-o gadgets in CoD to taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T19:36:35-08:00","id":785132,"title":"","content":"He's very good at developing Plans as equipment, and almost definitely has a whole bunch of interesting equipment to help him get the job done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T19:46:33-08:00","id":785133,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Hunter line would benefit from a straight out vigilante book.<br /> <br /> The existing books really dance around it, even with Slasher, with the idea that hunters sometimes uncover corruption or take care of more mundane criminals, but there's little Storyteller support for that kind of thing. Even the Tales from the 13th Precinct book spent more time on acting like a cop than dealing with crime.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to go with purple-glove Batman you could make him an Avenger.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.4thletter.net/wp-content/uploads/2011/08/pbnoe.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Most comic characters have been written long enough and been in enough Elseworlds or similar 'alternate universes' that you could portray them in a variety of game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T20:53:50-08:00","id":785159,"title":"","content":"Agreed. A vigilante supplement for Hunter is only fitting.<br /> <br /> I also had no idea that there was a version of Batman who killed. I guess his Bruce Wayne identity and the Bat Family are what keep him from turning into a full blown Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T21:11:29-08:00","id":785165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=785159#post785159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also had no idea that there was a version of Batman who killed. I guess his Bruce Wayne identity and the Bat Family are what keep him from turning into a full blown Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was early Batman, the stories were mostly retconned away as they tried to separate him from the dozen other characters he was inspired by. The purple was just a coloring error but it's a little trivia that purple-glove Batman is usually associated with the original more callous character concept, which is interesting as purple was really embraced by one of his most murderous enemies.<br /> <br /> As a werewolf fan, I find it easy to run the rogues gallery as claimed, urged or ridden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T21:45:28-08:00","id":785178,"title":"","content":"I don't think Mr. Freeze and the Penguin are essentially Slashers. The former just wants to bring his wife back from the dead, and the latter kills as a means to an end just like a normal criminal (he's even portrayed as sane most of time, but by no means harmless). Ivy is not always out for the blood of everyone who mistreats nature, and she even had a stable relationship with Harley at some point. It has also been said that she has the same power source as the Swamp Thing, so she could be a Deviant. Harley herself has left the Joker before, and has shown a desire to live a normal life. The Riddler is obsessed with proving his intellectual superiority first and foremost, and he even worked for the Gotham Police Department once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-13-2015, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T21:52:02-08:00","id":785183,"title":"","content":"I would be leery of giving the Bat 5 in everything.Despite how his meme has grown, even writers who lean hard into the &quot;Bat God&quot; interpretation allow the character to be vulnerable and have limitations, otherwise there is no drama. Especially in the a lower-power setting like Chronicles, I would be more inclined to give him 4's in most attributes (except Intelligence, Stamina, Resolve, and Composure). His primary crime fighting skills would largely be 4-5, but could easily be lower ( even at of the extended Bat Family, Dick Grayson is a better natural Athlete, Barbara Gordon is better at Computers, Cassandra Cain is an *arguably* better Martial Artist).<br /> <br /> While the &quot;Batman is the best at everything ever&quot; interpretation is valid, I prefer the character who has limits and triumphs in spite of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T08:37:45-08:00","id":785410,"title":"","content":"I like the ideas that are blossoming out of this. It just goes to show how many interpretations there are of the same iconic character that we've all grown up with. One thing is for sure, it would be possible to work Batman into a homebrew campaign using Hunter: the Vigil rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T16:19:09-08:00","id":785620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=785178#post785178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Mr. Freeze and the Penguin are essentially Slashers. The former just wants to bring his wife back from the dead, and the latter kills as a means to an end just like a normal criminal (he's even portrayed as sane most of time, but by no means harmless).</div> </div> </div> </div> Usually true.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ivy is not always out for the blood of everyone who mistreats nature, and she even had a stable relationship with Harley at some point. It has also been said that she has the same power source as the Swamp Thing, so she could be a Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends a LOT on the writer. A month or two after a story where she was protecting orphans, she was feeding people to a giant pitcher plant for lulz, and taunting them as they were being slowly digested alive.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harley herself has left the Joker before, and has shown a desire to live a normal life.</div> </div> </div> </div> Let's not forget that whole thing about Genii/Maniacs sometimes making disciples/apprentices. Joker's influence on Harley is great example of this. Harley HAS gotten better, though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Riddler is obsessed with proving his intellectual superiority first and foremost, and he even worked for the Gotham Police Department once.</div> </div> </div> </div> That IS part of the motive for Genii. That said, up until Flashpoint, Nigma really wasn't a killer, at least not often or intentionally.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T20:31:07-08:00","id":785716,"title":"","content":"On Converting Comic Characters into Game stats.<br /> <br /> The variance in capabilities and personality of these characters based on both the writer and incarnation of the character makes this sort of project tricky. Each of us has a interpretation we consider &quot;canon&quot;. Batman ranges from a man so hyper-competent he can fight gods (and win!) to a street level vigilante that can barely keep his city free of muggers and pimps.<br /> <br /> At least for the Chronicles, my instincts always say keep the scale of the system in mind. The Storyteller system can't really do most of the power tiers in a DC/Marvel style supers game. But the system can definitely model the section the &quot;mystery men&quot; tier of the Genre. Using a Batman that is more detective and vigilante than Super Hero (as well as similar characters such as the extended Bat Family, Marvel's Daredevil and the Punisher, or pulp mystery men like the Phantom or the Shadow) seem to be be just the proper level of power conceptually and tonally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T18:45:00-08:00","id":790613,"title":"","content":"I think the Air Of Menace Merit is more fitting for the Joker. Speaking of him, what Dread Powers does he have, if any? I believe has Dread Attack (Hidden Blades), Blast (Poisoned Joke Items), Lord Of The Manor (Prisons And Asylums), Transmutation, Cloak Of Authority, Twist Desires and Dement. The dot rating for each one can be changed as needed. He could also have <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/FanTheories/comments/230b06/the_joker_does_have_a_superpower/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>a specialized Omen Sensitivity.</b></a> On top of that, he has <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\"><b>Nightmare 3, Back For The Sequel and You Complete Me</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:04:21-08:00","id":829250,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about the possibility of having &quot;Purple Gloves&quot; Batman as an ex-Hunter who became an Avenger Slasher, and is on his way to becoming a Legend. That would turn our expectations of the character on their heads. As Bruce Wayne, he donates quite a bit of his immense wealth to humanitarian causes in Gotham and elsewhere, which actually helps to decrease the level of crime. The Batman persona is not glamorous for him, it is his skeleton in the closet. While wearing that suit, he is only barely aware that murder isn't justice. His relationship with the Joker would be the same, but even more tense. With no compulsion to spare criminals, the Joker would risk death every time he is caught. His goal would still be to give Batman the little push he needs to become a Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:06:34-07:00","id":896593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=790613#post790613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\"><b> You Complete Me</b></a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat makes me think of this: <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XE83DjolEAg\" data-code=\"XE83DjolEAg\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XE83DjolEAg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:53:29-07:00","id":900328,"title":"","content":"Be interesting for a genre-aware Joker that is a Legend to be trying to push/pull Batman to achieve the same sort of immortality so they could play their games forever, without letting Batman figure out a way to put him down for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:32:50-07:00","id":900449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=900328#post900328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be interesting for a genre-aware Joker that is a Legend to be trying to push/pull Batman to achieve the same sort of immortality so they could play their games forever, without letting Batman figure out a way to put him down for good.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThis has been implied to some extent or another in the comics. A few Elseworlds/possible future stories have featured new Batmen and new Jokers rising up to fight each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:04:22-07:00","id":901437,"title":"","content":"So can we agree that some of Batman's police allies are probably hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T21:49:22-07:00","id":901733,"title":"","content":"Renee Montoya went vigilante entirely, Josie Mac had some limited Second Sight abilities that would be fantastic for hunters.<br /> <br /> Crispus Allen was, briefly, host for the Specter, which was essentially a Rank 6 or higher Angel or Spirit.<br /> <br /> Gotham by Midnight even had what was basically an 'official' hunter cell, led by Jim Corrigan who was host for a much less personable version of the Spectre. They were the only cops in 'Precinct 13,' made up of the GCPD Detailed Case Task Force. They dealt with the very weird cases, had a few cops and some consultants, including a nun and a scientist, all touched by the supernatural. Scientist is right out of Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br /> Good comic, didn't last long as it should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-28-2016, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:19:04-07:00","id":902160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=901733#post901733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Renee Montoya went vigilante entirely, Josie Mac had some limited Second Sight abilities that would be fantastic for hunters.<br /> <br /> Crispus Allen was, briefly, host for the Specter, which was essentially a Rank 6 or higher Angel or Spirit.<br /> <br /> Gotham by Midnight even had what was basically an 'official' hunter cell, led by Jim Corrigan who was host for a much less personable version of the Spectre. They were the only cops in 'Precinct 13,' made up of the GCPD Detailed Case Task Force. They dealt with the very weird cases, had a few cops and some consultants, including a nun and a scientist, all touched by the supernatural. Scientist is right out of Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br /> Good comic, didn't last long as it should have.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't know all of that. Thanks for sharing. I also want to point out that there was a limited Elseworlds series titled The Doom That Came To Gotham, where a pulp hero Batman investigates Lovecraftian mysteries in the 1920s. It was created by Mike Mignola, the author of Hellboy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:00:34-07:00","id":902300,"title":"","content":"Watchmen's pulp human crime fighters seem extremely relevant for inspiration here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T15:25:41-07:00","id":902317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cowardly Scion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=902300#post902300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watchmen's pulp human crime fighters seem extremely relevant for inspiration here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well remembered. Rorschach is a good example of a Hunter with a dangerous Tell, and he could easily have gone Avenger Slasher. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:04:13-07:00","id":902374,"title":"","content":"Going back to the original subject: which members of the Rogues Gallery might be comparable to Deviants, which are more like minor Horrors who retain Integrity, and which are Slashers (Ripper or Scourge), and which fall into other categories? I don't remember any villain who really qualifies as a member of one of the major templates we have right now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For example, Killer Croc in later stages of his degeneration can be represented as a Mutant Slasher with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/155637-slasher-gmc-port\"><b>Nightmare 1 or 2</b></a>, Home Ground (Sewers), Advanced Iron Skin 2, Natural Weaponry 1, Monstrous Resilience, Regenerate 2 and Hunter's Senses (Humans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-28-2016, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T21:07:38-07:00","id":902472,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm hardly the most caught-up on the massive array of Batman rogues at this point in time, but, going by my own limited knowledge, this is what I'd suggest of the major names who don't immediately suggest just &quot;crazy human&quot; - for example, Penguin and The Ventriloquist are physically deformed (arguably, in the former case) and insane respectively, but there's nothing &quot;meta&quot; about them.<br /> <br /> The Joker: I think the most natural &quot;fit&quot; for this character would be a Slasher of the Maniac undertaking, which reflects his twisted combination of insanity and charm, reflecting how he somehow manages to keep amassing loyal followers despite his tendency to kill anyone around him. If you want to play with the whole &quot;I'm really an immortal agent of evil&quot; thing he tried to mindrape Batman with in the recent storyline that killed them both off, he could be spun as some kind of humaniform Horror.<br /> <br /> Harley Quinn: With her official &quot;power up&quot; at Poison Ivy's hands, I'd argue Harley Quinn is best suited for a Deviant basis. She is a cold-blooded killer, but it's not a driving compulsion like it is with other members of the Rogue's Gallery - she doesn't tend to rack up the constant bodycount her boyfriend and galpal do.<br /> <br /> Poison Ivy: When statting Ivy, one needs to remember there's at least two versions of the character to look at; the pre-modern version was a skilled botanical engineer and chemist who just happened to be a murderous vamp and ecoterrorist, and the modern version, which has given her full-fledged &quot;chlorokinetic&quot; powers. For the pre-modern version, a Charmer or Psycho (depending on how much you want to emphasize her insanity) with a unique &quot;immunity to poison&quot; trait, mutated plants (use the Horror rules) as mooks and poisonous lipstick as a Signature Weapon would be my recommendation. For the modern version, I'd go with a Deviant or a full-fledged Horror, depending on just what kind of powers Deviants actually get.<br /> <br /> Mr. Freeze: A Deviant without any question. <br /> <br /> Killer Croc: As GibberingEloquence stated above, a Mutant or Freak (depending on whether you want the &quot;deformed human&quot; or &quot;full-fledged gator-man&quot; version of the character) Slasher is probably the best fit for Killer Croc.<br /> <br /> Two-Face: I'd argue he quite neatly fits the Freak basis for a Slasher, the only problem being if you consider him murderous enough to qualify as a Slasher. He could just be handled as a low-Integrity human with a &quot;flaw&quot; that gives him a sharp penalty to some Social skills to reflect his physical deformity.<br /> <br /> Mad Hatter: I'd argue either a Maniac Slasher with a fixation more on mind controlling than killing or else a Deviant with a technological basis to his mind control powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T23:43:01-07:00","id":902513,"title":"","content":"Which Ventriloquist? There have been 3:<br /> \u200b1. Arnold Wesker, who beat a man to death to take the original Scarface* dummy from him. He was convinced Scarface told him to.<br /> 2. &quot;Sugar&quot;, a former mob wife who found Scarface after Wesker's death. Her crimes were largely about getting revenge after her husband shot her in the face and left her for dead. She was in the habit of rigging her dummies to explode.<br /> 3. I can't remember her real name, but a third Ventriloquist appeared in Gail Simone's recent Batgirl run. This disturbingly pale and emaciated young woman was a killer from childhood. She possesses telekinetic abilities, and her dummy, which looks like the puppet from the &quot;Saw&quot; movies, has built-in weapons. I can't remember her dummies name either, but she killed the performer at her birthday party, then modified his dummy.<br /> <br /> *The original Scarface was carved from the wood of the gallows tree at Blackgate Penitentiary, from which 666 men had been hanged. Cursed/haunted object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 05-29-2016, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T09:58:12-07:00","id":902778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=902513#post902513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. &quot;Sugar&quot;, a former mob wife who found Scarface after Wesker's death. Her crimes were largely about getting revenge after her husband shot her in the face and left her for dead. She was in the habit of rigging her dummies to explode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Peyton Riley, one of my favorites. Used by Tommy Elliot, mechanically a mortal or a Ripper Slasher, possible mother of Abuse, a Deviant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *The original Scarface was carved from the wood of the gallows tree at Blackgate Penitentiary, from which 666 men had been hanged. Cursed/haunted object? </div> </div> </div>I love that interpretation. Often it's just sort of a vessel for the 'Dummy's' madness.<br /> <br /> The Talons would be Deviants, as would Lincoln March and Bane, possibly. David Hill wrote a micro template for 'Lost Boys,' I think that would do Bane well. Zsasz would be a Slasher. The various Clayfaces Deviants. Professor Pyg's a toughie, I could see putting him in as a Maniac with his turning his subjects insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:37:53-07:00","id":902983,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd argue Zsasz as a Slasher... only problem is, what Undertaking? Being covered in scars and in love with flaunting them, he's clearly not a Charmer type - too obviously crazy. I'm pretty sure that his glass jaw in the games is canonical to the wider Bat-continuity, so I'd argue against the &quot;toughness emphasizing&quot; Brute. I don't know if I'd quite call his scars deforming enough to qualify for a Freak... but, with his game-verse self's stealth and deception, and his love of making intricate tableau out of his victims, he might qualify as a Genius?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:50:03-07:00","id":902990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=902513#post902513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*The original Scarface was carved from the wood of the gallows tree at Blackgate Penitentiary, from which 666 men had been hanged. Cursed/haunted object?</div> </div> </div> </div>He seems like something under the Bygone system. Dotless cursed artifact that attracts people with an inner rage to start using him as a voice for their Vice. He has a consistent personality, but when it comes down to it, Scarface is ultimately an echo of his puppeteer.<br /> <br /> In normal Batman, the question is whether the dummy's alive. In the CofD, the question is to what degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T16:59:43-07:00","id":903110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/784382-homebrew-idea-batman-in-the-wod?p=902983#post902983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd argue Zsasz as a Slasher... only problem is, what Undertaking? Being covered in scars and in love with flaunting them, he's clearly not a Charmer type - too obviously crazy. I'm pretty sure that his glass jaw in the games is canonical to the wider Bat-continuity, so I'd argue against the &quot;toughness emphasizing&quot; Brute. I don't know if I'd quite call his scars deforming enough to qualify for a Freak... but, with his game-verse self's stealth and deception, and his love of making intricate tableau out of his victims, he might qualify as a Genius?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://67.media.tumblr.com/49a2d896860c7c9be51d9f84ab0d7f34/tumblr_n61y1bJekT1r14zwfo2_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> The video game version is way different, it makes him seem more like a strung-out addict of some sort. In the comics he's like a serial killer who's always going through his phases. He sees everyone as zombies or corpses, wastes of flesh serving no purpose, not understanding or even really living. He sees himself as a predator, liberating them from their shallow existences. If you had to put him into one of the undertakings, he'd probably be a Brute. But a non-standard one, as he is actually pretty intelligent and very cunning. And physically, though he doesn't appear strong in many of his appearances, he's usually a tough combatant even for Batman. Surprise attacks really seem to be the best way to take him out. Part of the problem is that he isn't as 'showy' as a lot of the other villains, he doesn't want to make a statement or usually have a big show. He just sees someone, stalks them, kills them, and moves on to the next person.<br /> <br /> Someone compiled all his fights in a thread on another site, <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/mr-zsasz/4005-25091/forums/victor-zsaszs-fights-1615084/?page=1#js-message-13183267\" target=\"_blank\">here's his origin.</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/11118/111188754/4187284-2195318083-robin.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the TV show, Gotham, he's a pretty dedicated mob enforcer. Definitely weirdly psycho but probably not a Slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-29-2016, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:26:22-07:00","id":903163,"title":"","content":"Zsasz could be a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/333422-preservation-thread-predator-beast-undertaking\"><b>Predator</b></a>.<br /> <br /> Scarecrow is probably a Genius, and his fear toxin can be represented as various pieces of equipment and weapons that can cause Tilts such as Insane, Insensate, Broken and Spooked, depending on concentration and the victim. The fear toxin isn't implanted into his body in a way that significantly transforms who he is, so I'd say he's not a Deviant.<br /> <br /> Hush is likewise a Genius as demonstrated by his preternatural talents for medicine, strategy and deception. Rather than being an Avenger, he has the Obsessed Condition (Get My Revenge On Bruce Wayne).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:58:57-07:00","id":903228,"title":"","content":"Hush did have a glorious comeback in that regard.<br /> <br /> Jane Doe would probably be a Psycho with the Skinner Wolf-Blooded tell.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static1.comicvine.com/uploads/original/6/64770/1739104-janedoe9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mr. Bloom a Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-29-2016, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:50:26-07:00","id":911619,"title":"","content":"I really need to check the forums more often. I was actually set to run a Werewolf game set in Gotham before my group fell apart. I'm actually tempted to set my Mage game in Gotham (the core Mystery is that the Primordial Dream is closer to reality, sort of like in LA), though I don't think my players want that. Still, I wonder how long I could get away with using not-quite Batman villains. Hunter would probably be the best splat, whether or not you directly want Batman.<br /> As for what I was going to do, well, I wasn't going to have actual Batman, but Bruce Wayne's return to Gotham was going to be a subplot, along with a Year One style vigilante. Players would obviously be able to put two and two together, but what to do about him? Especially when their Totem, &quot;The Detective on Leather Wings&quot; takes an interest in this vigilante? I tend to give my players some hints and suggestions for what they'll deal with in a game, but one thing I kept under wraps is that the Detective was a spirit created by a young Bruce Wayne obsessing over his parent's death. So he was likely going to become a Wolfblooded.<br /> <br /> Other things include:<ul><li>The tainted Wound that formed in Crime Alley as everyone's depression pooled there.</li> <li>The undead monster (Solomon Grundy) stalking the underground (who can only die on a Saturday and must be buried on a Sunday)</li> <li>The pack's Wolfblooded:<ul><li>Awkward and quirky forensic analyst Edward Nigma (based heavily on the <i>Gotham</i> version) who just wanted to be helpful to the Pack, and probably saw his detective Werewolf as the coolest guy ever</li> <li>Rich and popular high school Mean Girl Barbara Kean (based slightly less on the <i>Gotham</i> version) who felt she owed her life to the Werewolf that bit her for saving her from a monster</li> <li>Jason Todd, the standoffish homeless kid with the Anger Issues Tell</li> </ul></li> <li>The Scarecrow, a powerful Fear Spirit that attacked the high school and now has its sights set on Barbara Kean... but first, it needs to Claim a host, and Johnathan Crane will do just fine</li> <li>The Falcone Crime Family, a group of Ivory Claws loyal to Steel Spire Falcon and headed by Carmine Falcone, though his Uratha son Alberto is jealous that his much more intelligent Wolfblooded father is running the show.</li> <li>A secret group of wealthy mortals with ties to the Strix. They provide the Strix with bodies to inhabit, and have secretly pulled the strings in Gotham.</li> <li>A no talent greasy and perpetually wet looking Nosferatu with a limp and a penchant for wearing three piece suits muscling in on the Falcone territory, because <i>Gotham</i> had a great version of Penguin.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gDh48J7fLhjE_8pWtu81_1rOLBPiqHwNFlayFbCKWL8/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the setting document</a>. Also the three preludes I ran before Ashley's player got overwhelmed by life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}